# The root build context is the whole repo, but the image only ships fyp-backend
# (see Dockerfile). Deny-by-default, because .dockerignore patterns are matched
# against the path relative to the context root: a bare `.venv` / `.env` /
# `node_modules` never matched fyp-backend/.venv (2 GB), fyp-backend/.env
# (secrets, and COPY fyp-backend/ . baked them in), fyp_web/node_modules, or
# fyp_flutter/build (1.2 GB). Listing what we want beats guessing prefixes.
*
!fyp-backend

# ...now drop the parts of fyp-backend that are local-only, huge, or secret.
fyp-backend/.venv
fyp-backend/.env
fyp-backend/.cache
fyp-backend/.pytest_cache
fyp-backend/**/__pycache__
fyp-backend/**/*.py[cod]
fyp-backend/tests
fyp-backend/*.bat
fyp-backend/*.db
fyp-backend/*.sqlite3
fyp-backend/Dockerfile
fyp-backend/.dockerignore
fyp-backend/README.md

# Kept on purpose: fyp-backend/ml/risk_model.pkl (analytics.py loads it),
# languages.json, alembic/, .env.example.
